  "body": "Release 0.24.0 (MINOR). The major is 0, so the two breaking changes bump MINOR. The release notes say \"breaking\" first.\n\n## Cut list\nThe cut line is 2026-11-18 17:33 UTC. The maintainer accepted this list.\n\nIn (all merged to `main` before the cut line):\n- #2533 (PR #2536)\n- #2436 (PR #2460)\n- #2480 (PR #2486)\n- #2403 (PR #2484)\n- feat #2253 (#1517, breaking: Pocket has no Adaptive, format 69)\n\nAlso merged since v0.23.0: #2555 and the other PRs in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\nOut (they wait for the next minor): #2515, #2506, #2310, #2134, #2149, #2092, #2122, #2352, #2096, #1713, #1798, #2256.\n\n## Known issues\nAt the cut line, no `P1` or `P2` issue was open (`gh issue list --search \"label:P1,P2\"` gave no result). Note: #2561 (P3) is a follow-up for the Contour tab bridge check. It becomes `P1` if a test shows a narrow bridge.\n\nNote: #1950 (P3, blocked) is open. 3D Pocket Adaptive on a whole model refuses Adaptive on the stock-ring levels with a note, and Offset rings cut those levels. The output is safe. The release gate skips its three pinned tests and checks that they still fail (see \"Cut gate fix\").\n\n## What this branch changes\n- `cargo xtask decisions --version 0.24.0`: 78 decision files go into `RECOMMENDED.md` under `v0.24.0`.\n- `RELEASE_NOTES.md`: the 0.24.0 section is on top of the history.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: 59 rows for 0.24.0, from the `Changelog:` lines of the merged PRs. PRs with `Changelog: none`, process bumps and test, CI or gate-map-only PRs have no row. No row had the `Unreleased` mark.\n- `cargo xtask release --version 0.24.0 --no-tag --skip-gate`: the version bump commit. It made no tag.\n\n## Cut gate fix\nThe first cut gate (run 44362577581, head 08aea2746) was red on 3 tests in 2 heavy lanes. All 3 are `#[ignore]`d tests that pin the open, blocked issue #1950. They were added red on purpose (16ffe937f, dc2e76926). No merge of this cycle made them fail.\n- `xtask/src/known_fail.rs`: a list of known-fail tests, each pinned to an open issue. The heavy lane of the target skips each test by name (`--exact --skip`), and the gate log prints `SKIPPED (known fail, #1950): <test>`.\n- Each skipped test gets its own release step that must fail. The step is ok only when all of these are true:\n  - libtest reports that exact test as FAILED.\n  - Its panic is in the pinned source file.\n  - A line of its panic message starts with the pinned text of its #1950 assert.\n- Any other result fails the gate: a pass, a renamed test, a crash, a compile error, or a failure for a different reason.\n- The gate reads the issue state with `gh issue view -R NeoTech/Camcraft` (time limit 30 s). A closed issue fails the gate. If `gh` cannot read the issue, the gate prints a note. The cut runner has no `GH_TOKEN`, so there the must-fail steps are the guard.\n- Local release run of the 3 must-fail steps on c3ee1723e: all 3 are \"known fail, red as expected\".\n- The decision is in `RECOMMENDED.md` under v0.24.0 (`#1950 - the release gate skips three known-fail heavy tests`).\n- Review notes fixed: four decision headings use `##`. The #1689 row keeps `(PR #1689)`, because no issue is linked to that PR.\n\nProcess change: yes. This PR changes `xtask/` and does not change `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`. The merging session runs `cargo xtask process-bump` after the tag.\n\n## Breaking changes\n- #1517 / PR #2253: 2D Pocket has no Adaptive strategy. Old projects migrate to 2D Adaptive (Spiral). Format 69.\n- #2441 / PR #2504: through-hole break-through includes the drill point length by default. Old projects keep `Tip`. Format 68.\n\n## Gate\n- The release tier runs on the cut runner: `cut.yml` with `stage=gate` (`cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots`).\n- Skipped: the pixel-snapshot lanes. This is the maintainer's standing decision: the snapshots have no value at a cut.\n- Skipped: the Windows arms of the per-OS pinned readings.\n\nChangelog: none (release mechanics)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
